---
title: Contact Us | Vermont Football Officials
description: Get in touch with the Vermont Football Officials — questions, or information on becoming an official.
layout: layouts/main.pug
# The Pug plugin hands page data to Pug as its options, and this page is
# rendered as a fragment that never sees the layout's doctype. Naming it here
# makes Pug write boolean attributes bare (`required`, not `required="required"`).
doctype: html
---

h1 Contact Us
p.lead
  | Have a question, or interested in becoming a football official in Vermont?
p
  | If you are thinking about officiating, start with 
  a(href='/information/becoming-an-official/') Becoming a Football Official
  |  — it covers what it costs, what you get paid and what is required. Then
  |  fill out the form below; that is the first step, and we'll get back to you.

//- A Netlify form: Netlify finds it in the built HTML at deploy time and
//- collects the submissions. `form-name` has to be posted with the fields, and
//- `bot-field` is a honeypot that only a bot would fill in.
form.contact-form(name='contact' method='POST' action='/contact/thanks/' data-netlify='true' netlify-honeypot='bot-field')
  input(type='hidden' name='form-name' value='contact')
  p.d-none
    label
      | Leave this empty: 
      input(type='text' name='bot-field' tabindex='-1' autocomplete='off')
  .mb-3
    label.form-label(for='contact-name') Name
    input.form-control#contact-name(type='text' name='name' autocomplete='name' required)
  .mb-3
    label.form-label(for='contact-email') Email
    input.form-control#contact-email(type='email' name='email' autocomplete='email' required)
  .mb-3
    label.form-label(for='contact-phone') Phone number
    input.form-control#contact-phone(type='tel' name='phone' autocomplete='tel' required)
  .mb-3
    label.form-label(for='contact-message') Why are you interested? #[span.text-muted (optional)]
    textarea.form-control#contact-message(name='message' rows='4' maxlength='1000')
  button.btn.btn-dark(type='submit') Send
